{"metadata":{"title":"Privacy Manifests","modules":[{"name":"Traffluent"}],"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article"},"abstract":[{"text":"What each module can collect, the required-reason APIs it calls, and the privacy manifest it ships, so you can fill in your app’s own manifest and privacy labels.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Traffluent collects nothing on its own. It records only the events your app tracks and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"context your app turns on: every kind of automatic instrumentation and every standard enricher is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"opt in. It sends records only to the destinations your app gives a delivery, to endpoints your app","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"names. None of it is used for tracking as Apple defines it: no module links what it records with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"other companies’ data, reads the advertising identifier, fingerprints the device, or works around","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the user’s consent or App Tracking Transparency. Every manifest declares ","type":"text"},{"code":"NSPrivacyTracking","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"false","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and lists no tracking domains.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each module that can produce data of one of Apple’s collected data types ships a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" declaring it. SwiftPM and Bazel both put it in a resource bundle named"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"Traffluent_<Module>.bundle","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", which Xcode and rules_apple copy into your app, where Xcode’s privacy"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"report finds it. A module your app doesn’t link adds nothing to the report."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","text":"Required-reason APIs","level":3,"anchor":"Required-reason-APIs"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No Traffluent module calls an API on Apple’s list of required-reason APIs, so every manifest’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is empty. The list’s categories are file timestamps"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryFileTimestamp","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), system boot time"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategorySystemBootTime","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), disk space"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryDiskSpace","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), active keyboards"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryActiveKeyboards","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") and user defaults"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"). The modules that come nearest:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"table","header":"row","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Module","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"What it calls"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Why none is a required-reason API"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence","isActive":true}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"swift-system’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FileDescriptor"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"open"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"read"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"write"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"seek"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"resize"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"close"},{"text":"), ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fsync"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"unlink"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FileManager"},{"text":"’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"createDirectory"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"setAttributes"},{"text":" (the file protection class), ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"contentsOfDirectory"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isExcludedFromBackup"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"It reads no file’s timestamps, size from ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"stat"},{"text":", or the volume’s free space: a segment’s size is the offset ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"seek"},{"text":" returns at its end, and the store bounds itself by the bytes it has written.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LifecycleTracking\/documentation\/LifecycleTracking","type":"reference"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FileManager.fileExists"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Data(contentsOf:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Data.write(to:options:)"},{"type":"text","text":" in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FileVersionStore"},{"type":"text","text":"; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ProcessInfo.performExpiringActivity"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It reads and writes the version file’s contents, never its attributes."}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/StandardContext\/documentation\/StandardContext","type":"reference","isActive":true}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sysctlbyname"},{"type":"text","text":" for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"hw.machine"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"hw.model"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ProcessInfo.operatingSystemVersion"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Bundle.infoDictionary"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Locale.current"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NWPathMonitor"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"identifierForVendor"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"None is on the list; ","type":"text"},{"code":"Enricher.vendorIdentifier()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is declared as collected data below.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The tracker’s record timestamps ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Date"},{"type":"text","text":")"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A session’s inactivity is measured between records’ wall-clock timestamps, not from the system’s uptime.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers","isActive":true,"type":"reference"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Date.now"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Wall-clock time, not boot time."}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations","isActive":true}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ContinuousClock"},{"type":"text","text":", the default clock of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"batch()"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The Swift runtime’s clock, which isn’t on the list.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GRDBPersistence\/documentation\/GRDBPersistence","type":"reference","isActive":true}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"GRDB","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"GRDB ships a privacy manifest of its own."}],"type":"paragraph"}]]]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Every other module calls nothing near the list. Of the packages Traffluent depends on,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"swift-system’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"Stat","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" API (","type":"text"},{"code":"FilePath.stat()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"FileDescriptor.stat()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") calls ","type":"text"},{"code":"stat","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"fstat","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"lstat","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"fstatat","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"statfs","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Traffluent calls none of it. If your app does, your manifest","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"declares the file timestamp or disk space reason it needs.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","text":"Collected data","level":3,"anchor":"Collected-data"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Every declaration below is ","type":"text"},{"code":"NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeLinked","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"false","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (Traffluent links nothing","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to the user’s identity), ","type":"text"},{"code":"NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeTracking","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"false","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and has the one purpose","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeAnalytics","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". A module declares a type only when it makes data of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that type itself; it is collected only once your app turns the module on and delivers the records","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"off the device.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"table","header":"row","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Module","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Data type"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"What it makes, once your app turns it on","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/StandardContext\/documentation\/StandardContext","isActive":true,"type":"reference"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Device ID ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeDeviceID"},{"type":"text","text":")"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Enricher.vendorIdentifier()"},{"type":"text","text":": the platform’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"identifierForVendor"},{"type":"text","text":", as a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"VendorIdentifierKey"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/StandardContext\/documentation\/StandardContext"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Other Diagnostic Data ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeOtherDiagnosticData"},{"type":"text","text":")"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"Enricher.application()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"device()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"operatingSystem()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"network()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": the app’s bundle identifier, version and build; the device’s model and form factor; the operating system’s name and version; and the kind of network connection.","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/StandardContext\/documentation\/StandardContext","type":"reference","isActive":true}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Other Data Types (","type":"text"},{"code":"NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeOtherDataTypes","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":")","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Enricher.locale()"},{"type":"text","text":": the user’s locale."}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftUITracking\/documentation\/SwiftUITracking"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Product Interaction ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeProductInteraction"},{"type":"text","text":")"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"trackScreen(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"ScreenViewed","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and the events ","type":"text"},{"code":"trackOnAppear(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"trackOnTap(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"trackChange(of:_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" track as the user moves through the app.","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/UIKitTracking\/documentation\/UIKitTracking"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Product Interaction"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The events ","type":"text"},{"code":"UIControl.track(_:for:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" tracks when a control’s action fires.","t